Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:35:47 -0330
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Vehicles (holtburger fork): Hellcat from AC items,
 armament, review fixes, GC + villa basements

Session 3 (2026-11-02; holtburger-web docs/vehicles-2026-11-01 DESIGN decisions 62-73).

- The Hellcat built from 55 retail parts (VehicleProfile: parts + roles); the retail stand-in is the
  cockpit tub (Bucket 0x0200043C at 2x) with the seat in it. HBV1 v2 (VehicleWire, tests + fixtures).
- Armament: six crossbow guns (one salvo per step, harmonized at 110 m, hits applied on arrival), six
  rails launching real Lightning Bolt spell projectiles (the vehicle as launcher, ItemSpellcraft 400,
  aim assist), one 2,000 lb + two 1,000 lb bombs (VehicleOrdnance: ballistic twin of the client's,
  blast damage with falloff, a retail Flame Bolt fireball, the Explosion event), rearm after 6 s
  parked, @vehicle rearm [all].
- Review fixes: positions clamped to landblocks 0-254 (seat, muzzle, bail); characters saved in the
  sky snapped to the ground at login (AirborneSaveMark, PropertyBool 9001); pilot / faller deaths
  handled on the world thread; combat, spells, Use and recalls refused while seated or falling; no
  boarding while falling; idle parked vehicles despawn after 10 min; the wide sight budget only for
  seated pilots; concurrent seated / falls maps; reused broadcast buffers; the armament warm-up off
  the world thread.
- GC: vehicle_defer_dungeons (vehicle-only dungeon landblocks bring up nothing) and
  vehicle_shared_cellstructs (CellStructCache); the promoted-MB [gc] stall line; run-ace-live.sh with
  gen0 + gen1 budgets of 16 MB per heap, DATAS off, 2 heaps, no affinitization, HighMemPercent 97.
- Villa / mansion basements under the flight path: House.SetLinkProperties caches the outdoor house
  5 s; HousePortal reads the root portal's location from the cached world instances instead of a
  full House.Load per access; the house-portal table and the outdoor-house query warmed at startup;
  the corridor's spawn warm-up fetches a basement's root landblock instances.
- Diagnostics: [HEAVYADD] link cost split by parent type; [VEHICLE][INBOUND] names an inbound
  message / game action holding the world thread over 30 ms while a vehicle is active.

Verified live on the laptop server: armament benches, review-fix bench (recall / melee refused while
seated, re-board, pilot killed in the air placed on the ground), a SIGKILL crash with the pilot saved
in the sky (entered on the ground after restart), sea-route GC benches. ACE.Server.Tests Vehicles 12/12.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
